/* book: lead: The spark must arrive at a crank angle, so the ECU works in crank degrees. It switches the coil on for a dwell time that stores enough energy, switches it off to fire the plug a set number of degrees before top dead centre (TDC), and retards that angle when the knock sensor hears knock. Spark advance decides torque, fuel economy, emissions and piston survival. */
/* book Figure 4.6.1: The worked example on a crank-angle scale. The 3.0 ms dwell is 54 degrees at 3000 rpm and 108 degrees at 6000 rpm, both ending at the spark 25 degrees before TDC; the dot is the pressure peak just after TDC. At 6000 rpm the previous spark and the new dwell fit inside the 5.0 ms gap with 0.5 ms spare */
